    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a challenging subject for me, but I appreciate its logical structure. While I don't excel in it like my favorite subjects, computer science and physics, I see the beauty in patterns and problem-solving. My father's background in engineering influenced my interest, though I struggle more than I'd like to admit.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, especially with complex problems or abstract concepts. The pressure to perform well, combined with my self-doubt, makes it stressful. However, I’ve learned to break tasks into smaller steps to manage anxiety. My low neuroticism helps me stay calm under pressure, but math still triggers some unease.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I haven’t used AI tools for math yet, but I’m curious about them. My high conscientiousness makes me want to learn efficiently, so if an AI could simplify concepts or provide step-by-step guidance, I’d likely find it helpful. Right now, I rely more on textbooks and peer discussions.",
